{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"naval-halfasleep-shorebird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Main is RED on the gating cell\n\nScheduled Test Suite run `33950878570` (2026-09-05 06:49 UTC, `headSha a33333b8709a`) failed the\n**gating** cell `build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)`:\n\n```\nFAILED tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py::\n       test_ac3_verifier_routing_gets_distinct_fresh_terraform_session\n    assert len(opened) >= 2 and len(set(opened[:2])) == 2\nE   assert (2 >= 2 and 1 == 2)\n```\n\nTwo sessions were opened, but they were the SAME session — `set(opened[:2])` has one element where\nthe test requires two distinct ones. The test's name states the contract: the verifier routing must\nget a *distinct fresh* terraform session.\n\nFour `sweep` lanes also failed in the same run (`macos full suite`, `py3.15`, `py3.14t`,\n`windows`). `sweep (windows)` is `continue-on-error` by design and is tracked by the Windows\nsupport-target epic; the other three sweep lanes are NOT yet triaged and may or may not share this\ncause — establish that rather than assuming it.\n\n## Prime suspect, stated as a LEAD not a finding\n\n`git log` shows the failing test file was last modified by **`25d1d683e55a` — \"Add probe_source\nTerraform grounding tool\"** (Gerrit change 2645), which also added the `probe_source` tool to\n`src/rebar/grounding/`. That change modified both the test and the module under test.\n\nTimeline supports it but does not prove it:\n\n    01:07 UTC   scheduled Test Suite  SUCCESS\n    ~05:xx      25d1d683e55a merges\n    06:49 UTC   scheduled Test Suite  FAILURE, in a test that commit touched\n\nA session-routing change that makes two calls share one session is exactly the shape of `1 == 2`\nhere. But confirm by bisecting or by reading the diff — do not assume.\n\n## It does NOT reproduce on a default local checkout\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py::test_ac3_... -q\n1 skipped in 3.86s\n```\n\nThe test opens with `pytest.importorskip(\"hcl2\")`, so it SKIPS wherever the `hcl2` extra is absent.\nCI runs it because that lane sets `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1`, which turns an `importorskip` that\nwould skip into a hard error. **Install the extra before attempting a reproduction**, or the test\nwill silently not run and a green local result will mean nothing — the same skip-is-not-a-pass\ntrap this repo has already been bitten by (bug `599e`, and the chromium tier in `337e`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The failure is REPRODUCED locally with the `hcl2` extra installed, and the reproduction is\n      shown failing for the stated reason (`1 == 2` on distinct sessions) rather than erroring or\n      skipping.\n- [ ] The cause is established by evidence — diff reading or bisect — and named. If `25d1d683e55a`\n      is NOT the cause, say so and name what is; a refuted lead is a valid outcome.\n- [ ] The gating cell `build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)` passes on `main`.\n- [ ] Whichever side was wrong is fixed on its merits: either the routing genuinely lost session\n      distinctness (fix the code) or the test's expectation is stale against a deliberate design\n      change (fix the test AND state why the old contract no longer holds). Do not simply relax the\n      assertion to make it pass.\n- [ ] The three untriaged sweep-lane failures (`macos full suite`, `py3.15`, `py3.14t`) are each\n      recorded as same-cause or different-cause with evidence. Do not fold them in silently.","id":"ac93-09f5-6004-44af","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"main is RED on the gating py3.13 cell: test_ac3_verifier_routing_gets_distinct_fresh_terraform_session gets one session where it requires two distinct"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788594014102265001,"uuid":"7919d733-24d2-44ae-9315-36ec479731f1"}